ADDRESS: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association
==================================================
The Washington DC Snowball Fight Association (DCSFA) is a loose group of residents of  [LINK: (Washington, D.C.) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington,_D.C.] , United States, who organize large-scale  [LINK: (snowball fights) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snowball_fight]  via social media when the city gets significant amounts of snow. [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-:4-1]  Initially organized by Michael Lipin and Ami Greener, the first large snowball fight occurred in  [LINK: (Dupont Circle) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dupont_Circle]  on February 6, 2010, after the region received more than 30 inches (760 mm) of snow during the  [LINK: (February 5–6, 2010 North American blizzard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_5%E2%80%936,_2010_North_American_blizzard] . [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-2]  [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-:0-3]  [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-Hatchet-4]  More than 5,000 people RSVPed to the snowball fight on  [LINK: (Facebook) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Facebook] , and around 2,000 attended. [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-:0-3]  [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-5]

The snowball fights have garnered local, national and international press attention and have become a local tradition. [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-:0-3]  [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-:1-6]  [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-:2-7]  [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-:3-8]  [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-:4-1]  According to co-organizer Denis Baranov, for the DCSFA to schedule a fight requires at least four inches (100 mm) of snowfall, with the snow neither too flaky nor too wet. [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-Hatchet-4]


# SNOWBALL FIGHTS AND LOCATIONS #

Following the first series of snowball fights during the record-setting  [LINK: (2009–2010 winter snowfall) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_North_American_blizzards_of_2010] , [LINK: ([9]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-WJLA-9]  DCSFA continued to organize events. It held large snowball fights in Dupont Circle during a  [LINK: (January 2011 nor'easter) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_25%E2%80%9327,_2011_nor%27easter] , [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-:1-6]  during the  [LINK: (January 20–22, 2014 North American blizzard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_20%E2%80%9322,_2014_North_American_blizzard] , [LINK: ([10]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-10]  during a  [LINK: (March 2015 winter storm) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March_2015_North_American_winter_storm] , [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-11]  and amid the  [LINK: (January 2016 United States blizzard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_2016_United_States_blizzard] . [LINK: ([12]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-12]

DCSFA organized snowball fights on the  [LINK: (National Mall) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Mall]  during a  [LINK: (March 2014 winter storm) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March_2014_North_American_winter_storm] , [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-:2-7]  [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-:3-8]  on January 13, 2019, [LINK: ([13]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-13] 
in January 2021 during a  [LINK: (nor'easter) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31_%E2%80%93_February_3,_2021_nor%27easter] , [LINK: ([14]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-14]  and again during a  [LINK: (January 2022 nor'easter) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_3%E2%80%934,_2022_nor%27easter] . [LINK: ([15]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-15]   [LINK: (Meridian Hill (Malcolm X) Park) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meridian_Hill_Park]  became the site of a snowball fight during the  [LINK: (February 14–15, 2015 North American blizzard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_14%E2%80%9315,_2015_North_American_blizzard] . [LINK: ([16]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-16]

The  [LINK: (January 13–16, 2024 North American winter storm) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_13%E2%80%9316,_2024_North_American_winter_storm]  brought two DCSFA events, one on January 16, on the National Mall [LINK: ([17]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-17]  [LINK: ([18]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-18]  and a second four days later in  [LINK: (Franklin Square) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franklin_Square_(Washington,_D.C.)] , the first time since 2010 that the group had organized two in one week. [LINK: ([19]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-19]  During the  [LINK: (January 5–6, 2025 United States blizzard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_5%E2%80%936,_2025_United_States_blizzard] , with up to a foot of snow forecast for Washington, a DCFSA snowball fight returned to Meridian Hill Park. [LINK: ([20]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-20]  [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-:4-1]

The DCSFA scheduled a snowball fight at the National Mall for January 25, 2026, during the  [LINK: (January 2026 North American winter storm) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_2026_North_American_winter_storm] , but cancelled the event due to poor weather. [LINK: ([21]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-21]  [LINK: ([22]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_DC_Snowball_Fight_Association#cite_note-22]


